<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<mei meiversion="5.0" xmlns="http://www.music-encoding.org/ns/mei">
  <meiHead>
    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title>Diffusa est</title>
      </titleStmt>
      <pubStmt/>
      <notesStmt>
        <annot>Transcription: Corpus Monodicum (Akademie der Wissenschaften und der Literatur Mainz / Universität Würzburg), document Pa 776-0194-2GS, https://stagedata.corpus-monodicum.de/mei/ec37732f-542f-47e2-864a-7ce8109e2706/Pa%20776-0194-2GS.xml, which transcribes the Graduale Synopticum (Universität Regensburg; database by Xaver Kainzbauer), no. 0194; © Corpus Monodicum. Pitches read an octave lower than there. The folio is the one with the complete respond and verse for the Octave of Christmas; that the Graduale Synopticum transcribes this occurrence is not verified. Neume division, shapes and facsimile zones: a close reading of the BnF scan of f. 18v (October 2026), written as Aquitanian neumes on one editorial line (F). Every note of the respond in the Graduale Synopticum has its mark on f. 18v, in the same order.</annot>
      </notesStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
        <source>
          <bibl>
            <title>Diffusa est</title>
            <idno type="siglum">F-Pn</idno>
            <idno type="shelfmark">lat. 776</idno>
            <ptr target="https://archivesetmanuscrits.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cc62232g"/>
            <idno type="cantus-id">g01397</idno>
            <note type="genre">Gradual</note>
            <note type="mode">5</note>
            <note label="manuscript" type="description">Gradual of Saint-Michel de Gaillac, 1050–1100 (BnF catalogue); Aquitanian notation. The gradual for the Octave of Christmas, f. 18v.</note>
            <note label="manuscript" type="transcription">Corpus Monodicum (Akademie der Wissenschaften und der Literatur Mainz / Universität Würzburg), document Pa 776-0194-2GS, https://stagedata.corpus-monodicum.de/mei/ec37732f-542f-47e2-864a-7ce8109e2706/Pa%20776-0194-2GS.xml, which transcribes the Graduale Synopticum (Universität Regensburg; database by Xaver Kainzbauer), no. 0194; © Corpus Monodicum. Pitches read an octave lower than there.</note>
          </bibl>
        </source>
      </sourceDesc>
    </fileDesc>
